    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is built for high-ceiling production today, led by **Jose Caballero** (75.83) and **Corbin Carroll** (74.71), our top two projected starters. **Jose Caballero** enjoys a significant platoon edge against the lefty Lopez, J, bolstered by favorable park factors that elevate his score well into the elite tier. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** is a primary target today; while his status remains pending, the combination of a favorable matchup against Miller, B and his leadoff-adjacent positioning in the two-hole makes him a cornerstone for our stolen base targets. **James Wood** (73.33) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (73.64) round out our heavy hitters, with **James Wood** benefiting immensely from the leadoff spot and a soft matchup against Canning, while **Vinnie Pasquantino** exploits a strong platoon advantage against Leiter.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical risks, most notably with **Gabriel Moreno** and **Seiya Suzuki**, who are currently \"Lineup Pending.\" While **Gabriel Moreno** maintains a respectable 57.03 score, his value is tied to his projected slotting in the four-hole. We are also keeping a close eye on **Kyle Karros** (62.96), whose score is heavily propped up by a massive 14% park factor boost, making him a high-reward play despite the lefty-lefty matchup against Ray. The tightest decision on the bench was **Austin Riley** (53.37). Despite his pedigree, his score fell short of our efficiency threshold against the tough Lodolo, forcing him to the bench in favor of our more favorable platoon configurations. We are also monitoring **Travis Bazzana** (39.92), who sits just below our floor due to the brutal L/L matchup, and we are managing the IL status of **Mickey Moniak** as we keep our depth players like **Zach McKinstry** on standby should the weather or lineup news turn south.",
